        "\\Omega=\\frac{S}{R^2}"
      ],
      "inMemoryNormalizedText": "Draw rays from a point to the boundary of an arbitrarily shaped region to obtain the conical region of space shown in Figure 134.\nIts solid angle is denoted by $\\Omega$;\n\nits boundary need not be circular.\nDraw a sphere of radius $R$ centered at the vertex. The conical region cuts out a curved patch of area $S$ on that sphere.\n\nThe solid angle is the ratio of this spherical area to the square of the radius:\n$\\Omega=\\frac{S}{R^2}$ (6.1)",
