        "I",
        "I=\\frac{\\Phi}{\\Omega}"
      ],
      "inMemoryNormalizedText": "Luminous intensity. Luminous intensity describes the luminous flux emitted by a source per unit solid angle in a given direction.\n\nFor the uniform-emission model used here, luminous flux $\\Phi$ within solid angle $\\Omega$ gives luminous intensity $I$ according to:\n$I=\\frac{\\Phi}{\\Omega}$ (6.3)\n\nIf intensity varies with direction, this ratio over a finite solid angle gives only the average intensity over that region.",
      "normalizationWouldChangeText": true,
      "sourceSnapshotPreserved": true,
      "sourceRefsPreserved": true,
      "embeddedSourcePreserved": true,
      "textMatchesAuthoredList": true
    },
    {
      "language": "en",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "sourceRefs": [
